---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Box + Pixel - Privacy policy"
  description="What boxandpixel.com collects, why it's collected, and what you can ask Box + Pixel to do with it."
>
  <Hero headline="Privacy" />

  {/* Drafted from what the site actually does today. Review before launch —
      this is not legal advice. If the site starts using a newsletter, ads,
      chat or new analytics, update this page in the same change. */}
  <Prose>
    <p class="meta">Last updated September 24, 2026</p>

    <p>
      This page explains what boxandpixel.com collects, why, and what you can
      ask Box + Pixel, LLC to do with it. The short version: the site measures
      how pages are used, and if you send a message, it's used to reply to you.
      Nothing is sold, and there's no advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The site uses Google Analytics to understand which pages are useful. It
      sets cookies and collects information such as the pages you visit, how
      you arrived, your approximate location, and your device and browser.
      Google processes this data under{" "}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">its own privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can block analytics cookies in your browser settings, or install
      Google's{" "}
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The contact form</h2>
    <p>
      When you use the contact form, it collects your name, your email address,
      and your message. The form sends them by email, through a service called
      Resend, to Box + Pixel's inbox. They're used to reply to you and nothing
      else. You won't be added to a mailing list.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by Netlify, which may keep standard server logs, such
      as IP addresses, browser type, and request times, for security and
      reliability.
    </p>

    <h2>Fonts</h2>
    <p>
      Fonts are served from this site, not from a third-party font service, so
      loading a page doesn't send your details to anyone else for that.
    </p>

    <h2>What you can ask for</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask what information Box + Pixel holds about you, and ask for it
      to be corrected or deleted. Email{" "}
      <a href="mailto:hello@boxandpixel.com">hello@boxandpixel.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this page changes, the date at the top changes with it.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
